															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mortos" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1705184); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1705184&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606984965" alt="Mortos" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1705184)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mortos" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1705184); return false;" >Mortos</a></span> <span class="odate time_1529669613 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Jun 2018 12:13</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3846153">
									

<p>The core idea here isn't terrible, though without any context (having not read any of the rest of your teams doomcon entries) there just isn't really much here to work with. Your containment procedures feel overly verbose, being longer than your actual description. You mention that people who have successfully had this thing removed from them still need to be locked up. Why? Can't they be amnesticised? Is there any lingering anomalous acitvity? Following the discovery of a successful treatment, they still have this huge dedicated facility for housing these things - why aren't they all just treated?</p>
<p>As others have suggested the interview just doesn't seem to do anything. It only has a couple of lines of dialogue that actually contribute anything and the rest of it is just introductions. The mention of this dragon seems to come out of nowhere and doesn't seem to be connected to the rest of it at all and the process of actually getting around to mentioning it feels forced.</p>
<p>I do like the idea of a tree whose seeds take people over, though I feel the tree angle is brushed over pretty quickly too; where did these trees come from? Is there anything weird about them? Do their seeds just grow into normal trees if they are planted in the ground?</p>
<p>I spotted some specific issues, which you may fix or ignore at your leisure.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">issues</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>they will be sent to Site-104 for <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">quarantine.</span> for quarantine until removal surgery can be performed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This basically reads as &quot;to Site-104 for for quarantine.&quot; Honestly, this kind of strikethrough for a single word is unnecessary. I'd just remove the strikethrough entirely.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Containment Wing-3378 is six thousand square feet in size</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Measurements in Foundation documents should be in metric.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>especially for someone who had been catatonic for several weeks.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why was this instance catatonic? I thought they were moving around reading books and watching tv.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

