			<div class="content" id="post-content-4088806">
									

<p>For the rules in taxonomy the first letter of the name of a specie (genus) must be capital letter, and the first letter of the second name (specie) with lowercase letter. For it, <em>legionella pneumophila</em> must be <em>Legionella pneumophila.</em></p>
<p>A SCP is supposed is a inform written for a specialist, in this case probably a medic/biologist/professional from the biological area, and for this is few probable that commit this class of errors.</p>
<p>The idea is good but not convince me.</p>
<p>No vote for now.</p>
<p><sub>Also, for some reason this make me remember the fungic infection in The Last of Us, and other similar works.</sub></p>

