				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nebuladragon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2838114); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2838114&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606984965" alt="NebulaDragon" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2838114)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nebuladragon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2838114); return false;" >NebulaDragon</a></span> <span class="odate time_1584734037 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Mar 2020 19:53</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4557311">
									

<p>Very mixed feelings about this. On the one hand, I quite like the idea of it; a fungal infection that takes you over has been done before, but these ones seek nothing more than to consume knowledge, for some unknown reason possibly relating to an information apocolaypse of some kind. Interesting stuff was suggested. I also like the description of how the virus takes over, some good body horror there.</p>
<p>However, the thing that puts me off most is that the tone is really lacking in the clinical department. With sentences like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>to be warned through our CDC contacts</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Containment Wing-3378 is six thousand square feet in size, and has been built with reinforced airlock doors</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>After two members of the security team had been thrown against the walls of the quarantine chamber with enough force to knock them unconscious</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These and more really break the illusion for me. There's also the fact that, as people above mentioned, the possibility of a wider story isn't expanded on enough to hook me. The interview looks like it will provide more, but it doesn't really, and what little is added doesn't connect up.</p>
<p>So while I like the idea, unfortunately it's just not written well enough for me. -1.</p>

							</div>

								
					
